# Firebase Standards

## Stack

- **Cloud Firestore** for persistence
- **Firebase Authentication** for sign-in (email/password, OAuth, or as specified by the project)
- **Official FlutterFire plugins** (`firebase_core`, `cloud_firestore`, `firebase_auth`, etc.)
- **No REST API**: do not add `http`/`dio` layers for app data; all remote I/O goes through Firebase SDKs or callable Cloud Functions only if explicitly required by the product

## Data layer

- **Datasource**: thin classes wrapping Firestore/Auth SDK calls (`*FirestoreDatasource`, `*AuthDatasource`)
- **Repository**: implements domain interfaces; maps Firestore documents ↔ domain entities; handles errors and maps to domain failures
- **DTOs/models** in `data/models/`; mapping in dedicated mapper classes or factory methods
- Use `Stream`/`Future` types consistent with domain contracts; document stream subscription lifecycle in BLoC `close()`

## Firestore practices

- Collection and field names in English, stable and documented in `data-model.md`
- Prefer shallow documents; avoid unbounded arrays; use subcollections for one-to-many when needed
- Queries must match defined indexes (`firestore.indexes.json`)
- Use transactions/batches for multi-document writes that must stay consistent
- Handle offline: expose loading/error states in BLoC; do not assume immediate server confirmation

## Security

- **Security Rules** are the source of truth for client-side access; never rely on UI-only checks
- Update `firestore.rules` with every schema or permission change; test with the Rules emulator
- Do not commit service account keys or production secrets; use `flutterfire configure` / env-specific options

## Authentication

- Auth state drives routing/guards in presentation (e.g. `Bloc` listening to `authStateChanges`)
- Domain use cases depend on `AuthRepository` abstraction, not `FirebaseAuth` directly
- Sign-out and token refresh edge cases must be handled in repository/datasource layer

## Testing

- Mock datasources in unit tests; use `fake_cloud_firestore` or emulator-backed tests when integration is required
- Run Firebase Emulator Suite for local integration tests when feasible
- Do not hit production Firebase from automated tests

## Documentation

- Document collection shapes and rule intent in Spanish in `data-model.md` (field names stay English in code and Firestore)
- Align new operations with `firebase-data-access.yml`; do not extend `api-spec.yml` (deprecated)
